[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is a 3/4 overhead view at a 40-degree angle, showing two matte ceramic plates placed side-by-side on an aged, dark oak wood table. The primary plate in the foreground is sharp, while the second plate behind it is softly blurred. Each plate features one salmon fillet coated in a golden-brown, crunchy layer of toasted chopped walnuts and whole-grain mustard, placed beside a portion of bright, lightly charred green asparagus spears and a scoop of fluffy brown rice. The salmon skin is visible at the base, with the flesh appearing opaque and flaky. The asparagus shows slight char marks from the broiler. Soft natural side light from a window on the left illuminates the textures, creating a subtle sheen on the mustard glaze. Props include a wooden fork resting casually on the table and a small, blurred ramekin of Dijon mustard in the background. Scattered on the surface are a few stray walnut crumbles and a single fallen asparagus tip. The scene captures a warm, lived-in home kitchen atmosphere with a cozy, golden-hour color temperature. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Includes slight natural imperfections like a small sauce drip on the plate rim, uneven browning on the walnuts, and a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image is indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
